            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>
                    To Gaius Matrinius Aurelius Antoninus, son of Gaius, of tribe Lemonia, most perfect man, 
                    crowned [priest?] of Tuscia and Umbria, pontiff of the Flavian clan, editor of most abundant 
                    spectacles and also of preeminent theatrical delights, aedile, quaestor, twice quinquennial 
                    duumvir for administering justice of this most splendid colony, curator of the republic of 
                    this same colony and first notable, on account of his meritorious benevolence towards them, 
                    the whole urban people of Flavia Constans [dedicated this] to their most dignified patron.
                </p>
